From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mercurious <dutch.money@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 12:17:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] zlatez: widen the A650 EARLY_Z_LATE_Z hang workaround
 past its D32S8 gate

Upstream a70d2af590db ("tu/a6xx: Work around D32S8 EARLY_Z_LATE_Z hang")
forces A6XX_LATE_Z for A6XX_EARLY_Z_LATE_Z + D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT +
fs_kill_fragments, with the comment "A630/A650 hangs with this combination
of states". That is a fragment-stage wedge on the exact GPU this fork
targets, and it is the shape of the ETK reference fault: an upstream 3D
draw whose FS fails to retire, after which the CP blocks at the next WAIT
and hangcheck reaps it there.

The ETK workload uses Z24S8, not D32S8, so the format gate is the only
thing keeping the upstream workaround off it. This adds two default-off
TU_DEBUG gears that widen that gate:

  zlatez     also cover D24_UNORM_S8_UINT (the ETK reference format)
  zlatezany  drop the format gate entirely; any depth format

It also adds a dimlog diagnostic that fires with no gear set, reporting
the first time the hazard state is reached and in which format -- so
"are we even in this state?" is answered before any gear is judged. This
matters because every previously falsified fork gear was a *resolve*
mechanism; this is the first candidate that is not.

Because both gears are a strict widening of an existing upstream
workaround rather than a new mechanism, a positive A/B result is directly
reportable as an upstream MR. Status on commit: BUILT, not yet validated.
See PATCHES.md and GEARS.md.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
index a91ae08..afbef8e 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
@@ -13,6 +13,8 @@
 #include "vk_log.h"
 #include "vk_render_pass.h"
 #include "vk_util.h"
+/* ETK Patch #7: vk_Format_to_str() for the zlatez dimlog diagnostic. */
+#include "vk_enum_to_str.h"
 
 #include "common/freedreno_gpu_event.h"
 #include "common/freedreno_lrz.h"
@@ -7885,6 +7887,37 @@ tu6_build_depth_plane_z_mode(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd, struct tu_cs *cs)
        fs_kill_fragments)
       zmode = A6XX_LATE_Z;
 
+   /* ETK Patch #7 — zlatez. Upstream's workaround directly above is gated to
+    * D32S8, but the hang it describes (A6XX_EARLY_Z_LATE_Z + a depth/stencil
+    * format + a killing FS, on A630/A650) is a *fragment-stage* wedge, and the
+    * ETK reference fault is that same shape on that same GPU with Z24S8: an
+    * upstream 3D draw whose FS fails to retire, after which the CP blocks at
+    * the next WAIT and hangcheck reaps it there. The format gate is the only
+    * thing keeping the upstream workaround off the ETK workload.
+    *
+    * Diagnostic first: under dimlog, report the first time the hazard state is
+    * reached and in which format, so "is this even the state we're in?" is
+    * answered before any gear is judged. This fires with no gear set.
+    */
+   if (CHIP == A6XX && zmode == A6XX_EARLY_Z_LATE_Z && fs_kill_fragments) {
+      if (TU_DEBUG(DIMLOG))
+         mesa_logi_once("[ETK zlatez] hazard state reached: EARLY_Z_LATE_Z + "
+                        "fs_kill_fragments, depth_format=%s depth_write=%d "
+                        "stencil_write=%d",
+                        vk_Format_to_str(depth_format), depth_write,
+                        stencil_write);
+
+      /* The gears themselves: a strict widening of the upstream workaround, so
+       * a positive result is directly reportable as an upstream MR.
+       *   zlatez    — also cover D24_UNORM_S8_UINT (the ETK reference format)
+       *   zlatezany — drop the format gate entirely; any depth format
+       * Both default-off. See PATCHES.md and GEARS.md.
+       */
+      if (TU_DEBUG(ZLATEZANY) ||
+          (TU_DEBUG(ZLATEZ) && depth_format == VK_FORMAT_D24_UNORM_S8_UINT))
+         zmode = A6XX_LATE_Z;
+   }
+
    if ((stencil_test_enable && depth_format == VK_FORMAT_S8_UINT) ||
        (ds_test_enable &&
         (fs->fs.lrz.force_late_z || cmd->state.lrz.force_late_z)))
